OUTPUT : { "ClaimDocType__c": "PLA", "CedantClaimNo__c": (1) Cedant Claim Number (2) Ensure the number identified is the reference assigned by the Originating Insurer (Cedant), not the Reinsurer's internal reference "CedantPolicyNo__c": (1) Cedant Policy Number (2) the unique identifier assigned by the primary insurer to the underlying policy "LossDate__c": (1) Date of Loss (2) Ensure it falls within the effective policy period and determining the correct underwriting year for reinsurance (3) YYYY-MM-DD "IssueDate__c": (1) Issue Date of the document. (2) Depending on the context, this refers to the date the specific report or policy was officially generated or signed. (3) YYYY-MM-DD "InceptionDate__c": (1) Inception Date (2) The date the insurance coverage begins. (3) YYYY-MM-DD "ExpirationDate__c": (1) Expiration Date (2) The date the insurance coverage officially ends. (3) YYYY-MM-DD "ClaimCurrency__c": (1) Claim Currency (2) The currency in which the loss is being estimated and reported. (3) Convert any currency symbols or names into their official ISO 4217 three-letter codes. "SettlementCurrency__c": (1) Settlement Currency (2) The specific currency in which the claim payment is actually made or will be remitted. (3) Convert any currency symbols or names into their official ISO 4217 three-letter codes "FXRateToSettlementCurrency__c": (1) FX Rate to Settlement Currency (2) This involves the numerical rate used to convert the Original Claim Currency into the Settlement Currency. (3) If the document does not contain, set `1` "LossDesc__c": (1) Loss Description (2) The summary must answer the "Who, What, Where, When, and How" of the incident in a structured format. - What : Nature of the loss (Fire, Flood, Machinery Breakdown, etc.). - Where : Precise location within the insured premises. - When : Date and time of occurrence/discovery. - How/Why : The immediate cause (e.g., short circuit, pipe burst). If unknown, state "Cause currently under investigation." "Summary": (1) The description of the claim. (2) The summary must provide a bird's-eye view of the loss, focusing on the "Bottom Line" impact and the immediate outlook. "TotalAmt__c": (1) Total Amount (2) You must distinguish between the overall loss and the specific financial liability of the insurer. "ExpRsvRem__c": (1) Expense Reserve Remaining (2) This represents the outstanding amount set aside for future loss adjustment expenses. (3) Ensure the value is for "Expenses" (e.g., Adjuster fees, Legal costs, Surveyor fees), not for the "Indemnity/Loss" itself. "LossRsvRem__c": (1) Loss Reserve Remaining (2) This figure represents the estimated unpaid portion of the actual loss (indemnity). (3) Ensure the value is for "Loss/Indemnity" only. Do NOT include "Expenses" (adjuster fees, legal costs). "LossAmt__c": (1) Loss Amount percentage (2) This should represent the total estimated value of the damage (Gross Loss). (3) Identify Gross vs. Net : - Prioritize the Gross Loss (100%) figure. - If only a "Net Claim" or "Settlement Amount" is available, clearly label it as such. "ExpAmt__c": (1) Expense Amount (2) This should represent the total costs paid or incurred for professional services related to the claim. (3) Ensure the value refers to **Expenses** (e.g., Loss Adjuster fees, legal fees, surveyor costs, laboratory testing), NOT the actual damage/loss payment. "LKShare__c": (1) Percentage of Participation for for the relevant Reinsurer. (2) IIf the document does not contain, please set null "Remarks__c": (1) "Remarks," "Notes," or "Comments" (2) These are typically miscellaneous points that do not fit into standard data fields but are vital for claim strategy. (3) Identification: Look for sections labeled "Remarks," "General Notes," "Adjuster's Comments," or "Further Information." (4) Subrogation & Recovery : Pay special attention to and highlight any mentions of "Subrogation" (recovery from 3rd parties) or "Salvage" (remaining value of damaged goods). (5) Pending Requirements : Extract any notes regarding missing documentation or information still required from the Insured. (6) Legal & Coverage Caveats: Capture any warnings or professional opinions regarding potential coverage disputes or legal complexities. (7) Verbatim Extraction: Record the remarks exactly as they appear in the source text to maintain the original nuance. (8) No Hallucination: If the Remarks section is blank or does not contain, state "No additional remarks provided." "InsuredOrigin__c": (1) Insured Origin (2) Insured Details including the legal name. "InsuredEn__c": (1) Translate Insured Origin into English. "LossLocation__c" : (1) Loss Location (2) The specific site where the physical damage or incident occurred including Building No., Floor, Room, or specific Facility Name "LossLocationEn__c": (1) Translate Loss Location into English. "LossParticular__c": (1) Loss Particulars (2) This should be a detailed list of the specific assets, property, or financial interests affected by the loss. "LossParticularEn__c": (1) Translate Loss Particulars into English. }
